  ;; ONE stream-parameterized verb across the four pure listener streams.
  ;; The four `register-(event|error)-listener!` facade pairs were REMOVED
  ;; (pre-alpha — no compat aliases); the always-on event-emit / error-emit
  ;; registries are reached via the `:events` / `:errors` stream here, and
  ;; remain addressable via `re-frame.event-emit` / `re-frame.error-emit` +
  ;; late-bind for internal consumers.
  ;;
  ;; FACADE vs HOME-NAMESPACE VERB — the DCE tier rule (rf2-rfid2x).
  ;; `re-frame.core/register-listener!` (`:facade? true` in the generated
  ;; manifest) is the APP-FACING call form. Each stream ALSO has a
  ;; home-namespace verb — the TOOL-EMBEDDING form (`:facade? false`) that a
  ;; dev-only tool preload uses so it never requires `re-frame.core` into a
  ;; production build (bundle isolation / DCE):
  ;;   :trace  → re-frame.trace.tooling/register-listener!
  ;;   :events → re-frame.event-emit/register-event-listener!
  ;;   :errors → re-frame.error-emit/register-error-listener!
  ;;   :epoch  → re-frame.epoch/register-epoch-listener!   (rowed below)
  ;; The normative rule lives in spec/Tool-Pair.md §"Facade vs home-namespace
  ;; verb — the DCE tier rule". BOTH call forms hit the SAME registries and
  ;; BOTH carry `:tier :tooling` — registering a listener is a tooling-tier
  ;; concern regardless of call form (per spec/API.md §Tier vs Status, which
  ;; cites `register-listener!` as the canonical `:tooling` exemplar); the
