  ;; =========================================================================
  ;; re-frame.ui.test — the compiled-view substrate's testing surface
  ;; (day8/re-frame2-ui; epic rf2-vxgfnd, Spec 004; contract in Spec 008).
  ;; Unlike its sibling `re-frame.ui` (a curated :cljs-only surface — its
  ;; runtime targets React), `re-frame.ui.test`'s Tier-1 surface runs
  ;; HEADLESS on the JVM (`render` builds the structural tree; text / attrs
  ;; project it), so it is JVM-INTROSPECTED — the generator classpath carries
  ;; day8/re-frame2-ui BUILD-ONLY (rf2-vxgfnd.200) and `re-frame.ui.test` is in
  ;; the generator's `jvm-namespaces`, giving the same authoritative
  ;; `ns-publics` existence + :kind + :facade? derivation re-frame.core gets.
  ;; The reader-conditional CLJS surface is reconciled by the 2mtte CLJS probe
  ;; (fully-rowed, BOTH directions), so neither host can silently expose an
  ;; extra public. The `^:no-doc` runtime half `render-form*` is dropped by the
  ;; generator's `public-vars-of` carve-out; the CLJS-only `with-root*` owner +
  ;; `with-root-outcome` (^:no-doc) are internal by classification.
  ;;
  ;; The blessed surface (epic rf2-n7jtp — minimized to what crosses a real
  ;; host boundary plus the two tree-ABI projections):
  ;;   JVM structural (S1): render (one grammar, one :sub-overrides option) /
  ;;     text / attrs. These four rows (with with-root) are JVM-introspected.
  ;;   CLJS mounted (S2/S4): with-root (binds the connected DOM container) /
  ;;     (flush!)/(flush! thunk) / (flush-presence!)/(flush-presence! ms).
  ;;     `flush!` / `flush-presence!` are CLJS-ONLY (no JVM React tree to
  ;;     settle) — their manifest rows live under `:cljs-only` below, NOT here.
  ;; =========================================================================
  ;; =========================================================================
  ;; re-frame.freehand — the Freehand view substrate's ONE public door
  ;; (day8/re-frame2-freehand; EP-0036, D001; contract in Spec 004).
  ;;
  ;; The namespace is a DOOR, not a layer. The descriptor
  ;; type, its constructor `declare-view`, the head classifier, the call
  ;; normalizer and the render body live in the INTERNAL
  ;; `re-frame.freehand.descriptor` and are not rowed here — they are absent
  ;; from the supported surface by construction, not by a `^:no-doc`
  ;; carve-out. A raw constructor on the door would mint a value that passes
  ;; `view?` and classifies as `:view` while carrying no view-id, no source
  ;; and no lowering, which is the one-declaration rule (D002) with a hole
  ;; in it.
  ;;
  ;; `.cljc` and host-neutral, so the JVM generator owns tier/kind via
  ;; `ns-publics` (see `jvm-namespaces`); the CLJS probe reconciles the same
  ;; rows against the live analyzer surface, FULLY-ROWED in both directions,
  ;; so an accidental public cannot accumulate on either host.
  ;; =========================================================================
  ["re-frame.freehand" "defview"]           {:tier :front-porch :owner "004" :status "EP-0036"}
  ;; `custom-element` (rf2-sv2oq, ruled on rf2-5gliq 2026-07-25) is the second
  ;; declaration form on the door: it declares which of a custom element's props
  ;; are JS PROPERTIES rather than attributes. ADVANCED, not front-porch — the
  ;; paved path never reaches for it, an undeclared element needs no declaration
  ;; at all, and an application writes one only where it drives a
  ;; property-accepting web component. Spec 004D §Template grammar owns the
  ;; declaration grammar; 004B §Custom elements owns what the classification
  ;; then MEANS at conversion, which is why the owner axis names 004D.
  ["re-frame.freehand" "custom-element"]    {:tier :advanced    :owner "004D" :status "EP-0036"}
  ["re-frame.freehand" "view?"]             {:tier :advanced    :owner "004" :status "EP-0036"}
  ["re-frame.freehand" "describe"]          {:tier :tooling     :owner "004" :status "EP-0036"}
  ;; `manifest` is the third inspection read: a compiled declaration's
  ;; crossing manifest as plain data (nil for an interpreted one). Tooling
  ;; data alongside `describe`, so it shares its tier.
  ["re-frame.freehand" "manifest"]          {:tier :tooling     :owner "004" :status "EP-0036"}
  ;; `check` (rf2-drpa3.182.6) is the read-only compile checker's PUBLISHED
  ;; name — the door's one SOURCE-level read, where every other verb here
  ;; answers about a value the caller already holds. It runs the build's own
  ;; analyzer over a file's `defview` declarations WITHOUT compiling them and
  ;; answers one report per declaration; the analysis, the report vocabulary
  ;; and the recovery ladders all live in the internal
  ;; `re-frame.freehand.compiler.check`, which is NOT rowed — `check` is the
  ;; published projection of it, deliberately thin, because a second judgment
  ;; on this surface would be a second grammar to keep in step.
  ;;
  ;; TOOLING, and the tier is a statement rather than a default. `check` is
  ;; not application logic and cannot be: it reads a source file on the JVM,
  ;; so nothing in a running application is in a position to call it. Its
  ;; callers are a REPL, a build, an editor/CLI projection or an agent doing
  ;; preflight — the "dev / inspection surfaces … not for application logic"
  ;; row of the Tier taxonomy exactly. It also sits with the two inspection
  ;; reads it belongs beside (`describe` / `manifest`), and the
  ;; restrictive-by-default rule settles the remaining doubt against
  ;; `:advanced`.
  ;;
  ;; JVM-ONLY, and rowed HERE in :classification rather than under
  ;; :cljs-only — the same placement `render-static` takes below and for the
  ;; same mechanical reason: it is a `#?(:clj (defn …))` on the `.cljc` door,
  ;; so the JVM generator owns its existence and `:kind` via `ns-publics`.
  ;; Unlike `render-static` it has no CLJS arm at all (it is not a macro and
  ;; is not `:require-macros`-referred): head classification is resolution,
  ;; resolution is JVM for both compilation targets, and a browser runtime
  ;; has no source file to read — so the verb is honestly ABSENT on the host
  ;; that cannot support it rather than present-and-throwing, which is the
  ;; policy `->react` and the behavior tool plane state in the other
  ;; direction. That absence is machine-guarded from the CLJS side too: the
  ;; drpa3.63 probe carries `re-frame.freehand` fully-rowed, so a `check`
  ;; that ever became a live CLJS var would appear unrowed and turn it RED.
  ;;
  ;; Owner 004D, not 004: the checker's laws, its report and its finding are
  ;; owned by 004D §The read-only checker (009 §The compile checker report
  ;; records only where the finding ids come from), exactly as
  ;; `custom-element` above names 004D for the grammar that owns it.
  ["re-frame.freehand" "check"]             {:tier :tooling     :owner "004D" :status "EP-0036"}
  ;; `render-static` (rf2-drpa3.112, EP-0036 F5) is the Freehand server render
  ;; verb: `(v/render-static [view {…}])` compiles the LITERAL root form to the
  ;; versioned JVM structural tree and folds it to an inert HTML string through
  ;; the LATE-resolved `re-frame.ssr/emit-ui-tree` seam. UNLIKE mount /
  ;; hydrate-root / unmount! (the CLJS-only browser verbs, carried under
  ;; `:cljs-only` because a DOM node is), render-static is a JVM-only `#?(:clj
  ;; (defmacro …))` on the `.cljc` door — so the generator owns its kind via
  ;; `ns-publics` (`:macro`) exactly like `defview`, and it is rowed HERE, in
  ;; :classification, NOT under :cljs-only. A bare classification key is
  ;; namespace-qualified, so it never collides with the donor `re-frame.ui`
  ;; verb of the same name. Spec 011 owns the server render path.
  ["re-frame.freehand" "render-static"]     {:tier :advanced    :owner "011" :status "EP-0036"}
  ;; The paved path's render-only reactive read. The subscription law lives in
  ;; Spec 006 (D005), so the row is owned there even though the verb rides the
  ;; Freehand door — front-porch, the everyday read primitive paired with
  ;; `defview`.
  ["re-frame.freehand" "sub"]               {:tier :front-porch :owner "006" :status "EP-0036"}
  ["re-frame.freehand" "event"]             {:tier :advanced    :owner "004" :status "EP-0036"}
  ["re-frame.freehand" "handler"]           {:tier :advanced    :owner "004" :status "EP-0036"}
  ["re-frame.freehand" "render-fn"]         {:tier :advanced    :owner "004" :status "EP-0036"}
  ["re-frame.freehand" "raw-fn"]            {:tier :advanced    :owner "004" :status "EP-0036"}
  ;; Render slots (EP-0036 F5a). `render-fn` above declares the content and
  ;; `slot` invokes it, and the pair is COMMON grammar: a seq form the compiled
  ;; analyzer recognises, an ordinary macro / function call an interpreted body
  ;; runs. `slot` is a real function on the door rather than a resolution-only
  ;; stub, because the interpreted mode genuinely invokes it — and the compiled
  ;; analyzer discriminates the grammar BY RESOLUTION, so the var has to exist
